    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1038/ngeo1797",
    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "Global-scale climate reconstructions often mask significant regional temperature variations, hindering the ability to quantify continental-scale patterns over the past two millennia and distinguish the background range of natural variability from recent anthropogenic impacts.",
    "method": "We reconstructed past temperatures for seven continental-scale regions using a global dataset of proxy records to elucidate spatio-temporal patterns of climate variability during the past two millennia.",
    "task": "The task is to reconstruct temperature variability for seven continental-scale regions over the past one to two millennia using a global compilation of proxy climate records to elucidate spatio-temporal patterns of past climate change.",
